 workflow that preserves lineage, rewrites owned [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]references, and keeps old IDs and hosted URLs working as [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]compatibility aliases without changing immutable commit history.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]4[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plans:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]historical_bead_reprefix.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202608/historical_bead_reprefix.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-ei[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-ei/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Rust bead identity and alias primitive[/bold #D7AFFF]                        [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]core-reprefix[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-reprefix: add the Rust-backed collision-safe full-store bead ID [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]mapping, canonical event/projection rewrite, persistent old-ID aliases, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]exact token rewriting, PyO3 bindings, and mixed-prefix lineage tests.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Plan, ChangeSpec, and compatibility-page rewriters[/bold #D7AFFF]            [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]reference-rewriters[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core-reprefix[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]reference-rewriters: add codec-driven plan and ChangeSpec rewrite [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]planners plus canonical and old-ID compatibility bead pages, with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]exact-match audit and malformed-input coverage.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Historical agent identity and chat migration[/bold #D7AFFF]         